window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["django"]=[{"id":"django-f0001","card":"q-django-001-overview","sec":"django-s001","q":"What project is built throughout the Django Essential Training course?","a":"<p><strong>SmartNotes</strong>: per-user notes with CRUD, likes, public/private sharing and auth.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0002","card":"q-django-001-overview","sec":"django-s001","q":"Which features does the SmartNotes project cover?","a":"<p>CRUD, likes, public/private sharing and authentication, with notes that belong to each user.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0003","card":"q-django-002-1-django-basics-project-and-mvt","sec":"django-s002","q":"What is Django, and what are its main selling points?","a":"<p>Django is an open source Python web framework. It is fast to build with, has strong built-in security and has built-in user authentication.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0004","card":"q-django-002-1-django-basics-project-and-mvt","sec":"django-s002","q":"Why does Django have excellent documentation, and why does that matter?","a":"<p>Django came out of a newspaper. Learning to find answers in the docs (https://docs.djangoproject.com/) is itself a career skill.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0005","card":"q-django-002-1-django-basics-project-and-mvt","sec":"django-s002","q":"What are the prerequisites for the Django course?","a":"<p>Python 3.8+ (virtualenv), Django 3.2+ and HTTP basics.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0006","card":"q-django-002-1-django-basics-project-and-mvt","sec":"django-s002","q":"Which commands install Django, create the SmartNotes project and start the dev server?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install Django\ndjango-admin startproject smartnotes .   # manage.py + smartnotes/ config folder\npython manage.py runserver               # http://localhost:8000</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0007","card":"q-django-002-1-django-basics-project-and-mvt","sec":"django-s002","q":"In a Django project, what do <code>manage.py</code>, <code>settings.py</code> and <code>urls.py</code> do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>manage.py</code>: entry point (run server, DB tasks).</li>\n  <li><code>settings.py</code>: config (<code>DEBUG</code>, <code>INSTALLED_APPS</code>, database).</li>\n  <li><code>urls.py</code>: URL routing.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0008","card":"q-django-002-1-django-basics-project-and-mvt","sec":"django-s002","q":"What does <code>DEBUG = True</code> do in Django, and what does an undefined path show?","a":"<p>It turns on detailed error pages. An undefined path shows a 404 page listing the available URLs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0009","card":"q-django-003-apps-and-mvt","sec":"django-s003","q":"How are Django projects split up, and which command creates a new app called <code>home</code>?","a":"<p>Projects are split into <strong>apps</strong> with clear boundaries.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>django-admin startapp home</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0010","card":"q-django-003-apps-and-mvt","sec":"django-s003","q":"How do you register a custom app such as <code>home</code> in a Django project?","a":"<p>Add it to <code>INSTALLED_APPS</code> in <code>settings.py</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>INSTALLED_APPS = [\n    &#x27;django.contrib.admin&#x27;,\n    &#x27;django.contrib.auth&#x27;,\n    # ...\n    &#x27;home&#x27;,   # custom apps\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0011","card":"q-django-003-apps-and-mvt","sec":"django-s003","q":"In Django's MVT pattern, what is the responsibility of the Model, View and Template?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Model</td><td>Data and how it is stored</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>View</td><td>Receives a request, returns a response (the \"controller\" role)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Template</td><td>Renders data into HTML</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0012","card":"q-django-003-apps-and-mvt","sec":"django-s003","q":"What is a minimal Django view that returns \"Hello, world!\"?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.http import HttpResponse\n\ndef home(request):\n    return HttpResponse(&#x27;Hello, world!&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0013","card":"q-django-003-apps-and-mvt","sec":"django-s003","q":"What is the request flow in Django?","a":"<p>The URL is requested, Django matches it in <code>urls.py</code>, calls the view, and the view returns the response.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0014","card":"q-django-004-templates-and-dtl","sec":"django-s004","q":"What is the Django convention for where templates live, and why?","a":"<p><code>app/templates/app/file.html</code>. The inner folder named after the app tells you which app a template belongs to.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0015","card":"q-django-004-templates-and-dtl","sec":"django-s004","q":"How do you render a template with a variable from a Django view?","a":"<p>Use <code>render(request, template_name, context_dict)</code>. The context dict passes variables from the view to the template.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from datetime import datetime\nfrom django.shortcuts import render\n\ndef home(request):\n    return render(request, &#x27;home/welcome.html&#x27;, {&#x27;today&#x27;: datetime.today()})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0016","card":"q-django-004-templates-and-dtl","sec":"django-s004","q":"How do you output a context variable such as <code>today</code> in a Django template?","a":"<p>Write <code>{{ today }}</code>. <code>{{ var }}</code> outputs the variable passed in the context dict.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;p&gt;Today is {{ today }}&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0017","card":"q-django-005-self-contained-apps-include","sec":"django-s005","q":"What makes a Django app self-contained, and how do you achieve it?","a":"<p>You can delete its folder and the project still works. Give each app its own <code>urls.py</code> and reference it by string in the project URLs, so there is no import dependency.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0018","card":"q-django-005-self-contained-apps-include","sec":"django-s005","q":"What does the app-level <code>home/urls.py</code> look like for a <code>home</code> view?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.urls import path\nfrom home import views\n\nurlpatterns = [\n    path(&#x27;home&#x27;, views.home),\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0019","card":"q-django-005-self-contained-apps-include","sec":"django-s005","q":"How does the project <code>smartnotes/urls.py</code> pull in the URLs of the <code>home</code> app?","a":"<p>It uses <code>include</code> with a string.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.urls import path, include\n\nurlpatterns = [\n    path(&#x27;&#x27;, include(&#x27;home.urls&#x27;)),\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0020","card":"q-django-006-2-admin-and-built-in-auth","sec":"django-s006","q":"What is the Django admin site and where is it?","a":"<p>It ships with Django at <code>/admin/</code> and gives staff a web UI over the data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0021","card":"q-django-006-2-admin-and-built-in-auth","sec":"django-s006","q":"What do red warnings at <code>runserver</code> mean in Django, and which commands fix them and create an admin user?","a":"<p>Migrations are not applied yet.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python manage.py migrate           # creates tables for admin/auth apps\npython manage.py createsuperuser   # Django enforces password strength; never bypass in production</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0022","card":"q-django-006-2-admin-and-built-in-auth","sec":"django-s006","q":"What can you do in the Django admin?","a":"<p>List, filter, search, create/edit/delete (with confirmation) and see the action history. Users and Groups are real DB tables.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0023","card":"q-django-006-2-admin-and-built-in-auth","sec":"django-s006","q":"How does Django store passwords?","a":"<p>Hashed. You only see random characters. Admin enforces password validation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0024","card":"q-django-006-2-admin-and-built-in-auth","sec":"django-s006","q":"How can a system without user input, such as a blog, use Django?","a":"<p>Create all the data in admin and use views only to display it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0025","card":"q-django-007-protecting-a-view","sec":"django-s007","q":"How do you protect a function-based view so only logged-in users see it?","a":"<p>Decorate it with <code>@login_required</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.contrib.auth.decorators import login_required\n\n@login_required(login_url=&#x27;/admin&#x27;)\ndef authorized(request):\n    return render(request, &#x27;home/authorized.html&#x27;, {})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0026","card":"q-django-007-protecting-a-view","sec":"django-s007","q":"What happens with <code>@login_required</code> when the user is logged in and when not?","a":"<p>Logged in: the page renders. Not logged in: without <code>login_url</code> the result is a 404; with <code>login_url</code> the user is redirected to the login page.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0027","card":"q-django-007-protecting-a-view","sec":"django-s007","q":"How is the <code>authorized</code> view routed in <code>home/urls.py</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>path(&#x27;authorized&#x27;, views.authorized),   # home/urls.py</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0028","card":"q-django-008-3-models-migrations-and-orm","sec":"django-s008","q":"What is the Django ORM, and what is the workflow for a model?","a":"<p>Each model class is a table and each class attribute is a column. The workflow is: define the model, <code>makemigrations</code>, <code>migrate</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0029","card":"q-django-008-3-models-migrations-and-orm","sec":"django-s008","q":"How do you define the <code>Notes</code> model with a title, text and creation time?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.db import models\n\nclass Notes(models.Model):\n    title = models.CharField(max_length=200)\n    text = models.TextField()\n    created = models.DateTimeField(auto_now_add=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0030","card":"q-django-008-3-models-migrations-and-orm","sec":"django-s008","q":"What do <code>CharField</code>, <code>TextField</code> and <code>DateTimeField</code> do in a Django model?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>CharField</code></td><td>Short text, <code>max_length</code> required</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>TextField</code></td><td>Unlimited text</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>DateTimeField</code></td><td><code>auto_now_add=True</code> fills it on creation</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0031","card":"q-django-008-3-models-migrations-and-orm","sec":"django-s008","q":"Which two commands create and apply migrations in Django?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python manage.py makemigrations   # writes notes/migrations/0001_initial.py (a recipe)\npython manage.py migrate          # applies it to the DB</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0032","card":"q-django-008-3-models-migrations-and-orm","sec":"django-s008","q":"What is a Django migration file, and when does the DB change?","a":"<p>A list of operations. The DB is unchanged until <code>migrate</code>. The first migration is always <code>0001_initial</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0033","card":"q-django-008-3-models-migrations-and-orm","sec":"django-s008","q":"How do you create the <code>notes</code> app?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>django-admin startapp notes     # then add &#x27;notes&#x27; to INSTALLED_APPS</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0034","card":"q-django-009-registering-a-model-in-admin","sec":"django-s009","q":"Why does a new model not show up in Django admin, and how do you register <code>Notes</code>?","a":"<p>New models do not appear in admin automatically. Register them in <code>admin.py</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.contrib import admin\nfrom . import models\n\nclass NotesAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):\n    list_display = (&#x27;title&#x27;,)\n\nadmin.site.register(models.Notes, NotesAdmin)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0035","card":"q-django-009-registering-a-model-in-admin","sec":"django-s009","q":"What does <code>list_display</code> do on a Django <code>ModelAdmin</code>?","a":"<p>It controls the columns shown. Without it, rows show as \"Notes object (1)\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0036","card":"q-django-009-registering-a-model-in-admin","sec":"django-s009","q":"How configurable is Django admin?","a":"<p>Highly configurable, for example read-only fields and staff-only writes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0037","card":"q-django-010-django-shell-and-querysets","sec":"django-s010","q":"How do you open the Django shell?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python manage.py shell</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0038","card":"q-django-010-django-shell-and-querysets","sec":"django-s010","q":"In the Django shell, how do you fetch one note by primary key, list all notes and create a note?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from notes.models import Notes\n\nmynote = Notes.objects.get(pk=1)       # single object; mynote.title, mynote.text\nNotes.objects.all()                    # QuerySet (&quot;a list with superpowers&quot;)\nnew_note = Notes.objects.create(title=&quot;A second note&quot;, text=&quot;This is a second note&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0039","card":"q-django-010-django-shell-and-querysets","sec":"django-s010","q":"What is a Django QuerySet?","a":"<p>The result of <code>.all()</code>, <code>.filter()</code> or <code>.exclude()</code>: \"a list with superpowers\". QuerySets chain.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0040","card":"q-django-010-django-shell-and-querysets","sec":"django-s010","q":"What does each ORM method return: <code>.get(pk=1)</code>, <code>.all()</code>, <code>.filter()</code>, <code>.exclude()</code>, <code>.create(...)</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>.get(pk=1)</code></td><td>One object (raises <code>DoesNotExist</code> if missing)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>.all()</code>, <code>.filter()</code>, <code>.exclude()</code></td><td>QuerySet</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>.create(...)</code></td><td>New saved object</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0041","card":"q-django-010-django-shell-and-querysets","sec":"django-s010","q":"How do you filter notes whose title starts with \"My\" or whose text contains \"Django\" case-insensitively?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Notes.objects.filter(title__startswith=&#x27;My&#x27;)\nNotes.objects.filter(text__icontains=&#x27;Django&#x27;)     # case-insensitive contains</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0042","card":"q-django-010-django-shell-and-querysets","sec":"django-s010","q":"How do you exclude notes in the ORM, and how do you chain filter and exclude?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Notes.objects.exclude(text__icontains=&#x27;Django&#x27;)\nNotes.objects.filter(text__icontains=&#x27;Django&#x27;).exclude(title__icontains=&#x27;Django&#x27;)  # chained</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0043","card":"q-django-010-django-shell-and-querysets","sec":"django-s010","q":"What is the syntax for ORM lookups?","a":"<p><code>field__lookup</code>, with a double underscore. QuerySets chain.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0044","card":"q-django-010-django-shell-and-querysets","sec":"django-s010","q":"What do the Django lookups <code>__exact</code>, <code>__icontains</code>, <code>__startswith</code>, <code>__gt</code>, <code>__gte</code>, <code>__lt</code> and <code>__in</code> mean?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Lookup</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>__exact</code></td><td>Exact match</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>__icontains</code></td><td>Case-insensitive contains</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>__startswith</code></td><td>Starts with</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>__gt</code>, <code>__gte</code>, <code>__lt</code></td><td>Comparisons</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>__in</code></td><td>In a list (<code>id__in=[1, 2, 3]</code>)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0045","card":"q-django-011-adding-a-field-to-an-existing-model-like","sec":"django-s011","q":"Why use <code>PositiveSmallIntegerField</code> instead of <code>IntegerField</code> for a likes counter in Django?","a":"<p><code>IntegerField</code> (about ±2 billion) is oversized and allows negatives. <code>PositiveSmallIntegerField</code> (0 to 32,767) fits a likes counter and needs no negative-value validation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0046","card":"q-django-011-adding-a-field-to-an-existing-model-like","sec":"django-s011","q":"How do you add a likes field to the <code>Notes</code> model, and why <code>default=0</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>likes = models.PositiveSmallIntegerField(default=0)</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>default=0</code> gives existing rows a value.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0047","card":"q-django-011-adding-a-field-to-an-existing-model-like","sec":"django-s011","q":"After adding the <code>likes</code> field to <code>Notes</code>, what do you run and what migration is created?","a":"<p>Run <code>makemigrations</code> (creates <code>0002_notes_likes.py</code>, which depends on 0001) and then <code>migrate</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0048","card":"q-django-012-4-dynamic-pages-list-and-detail","sec":"django-s012","q":"How do you write a function-based list view for notes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from . import models\n\ndef list(request):\n    all_notes = models.Notes.objects.all()\n    return render(request, &#x27;notes/notes_list.html&#x27;, {&#x27;notes&#x27;: all_notes})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0049","card":"q-django-012-4-dynamic-pages-list-and-detail","sec":"django-s012","q":"How do the notes URLs get the <code>smart/</code> prefix in Django?","a":"<p>The app <code>notes/urls.py</code> has <code>path('notes', views.list)</code>, and the project <code>smartnotes/urls.py</code> includes it under <code>smart/</code>, giving <code>smart/notes</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>urlpatterns = [\n    path(&#x27;smart/&#x27;, include(&#x27;notes.urls&#x27;)),\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0050","card":"q-django-012-4-dynamic-pages-list-and-detail","sec":"django-s012","q":"How do you loop over notes in a Django template?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;ul&gt;\n  {% for note in notes %}\n    &lt;li&gt;{{ note.title }}&lt;/li&gt;\n  {% endfor %}\n&lt;/ul&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0051","card":"q-django-012-4-dynamic-pages-list-and-detail","sec":"django-s012","q":"In Django templates, what are <code>{% ... %}</code> and <code>{{ ... }}</code> used for?","a":"<p><code>{% ... %}</code> is for logic (loops, conditionals). <code>{{ ... }}</code> is for values.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0052","card":"q-django-013-detail-view-with-a-path-parameter","sec":"django-s013","q":"How do you write a function-based detail view that returns a 404 for a missing note?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.http import Http404\n\ndef detail(request, pk):\n    try:\n        note = models.Notes.objects.get(pk=pk)\n    except models.Notes.DoesNotExist:\n        raise Http404(&quot;Note doesn&#x27;t exist.&quot;)\n    return render(request, &#x27;notes/notes_detail.html&#x27;, {&#x27;note&#x27;: note})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0053","card":"q-django-013-detail-view-with-a-path-parameter","sec":"django-s013","q":"What does <code>&lt;int:pk&gt;</code> mean in a Django URL pattern?","a":"<p>An integer is captured and passed to the view.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>path(&#x27;notes/&lt;int:pk&gt;&#x27;, views.detail),   # &lt;int:pk&gt;: integer captured and passed to the view</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0054","card":"q-django-013-detail-view-with-a-path-parameter","sec":"django-s013","q":"What happens in Django if <code>DoesNotExist</code> is not handled, and what does catching it give?","a":"<p>Unhandled, it gives a <strong>500</strong> (with the full traceback only when <code>DEBUG = True</code>). Catching it and raising <code>Http404</code> gives a controlled <strong>404</strong>. A custom 404 template is possible.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0055","card":"q-django-013-detail-view-with-a-path-parameter","sec":"django-s013","q":"How does a Django detail template show a note's title and text?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;h1&gt;{{ note.title }}&lt;/h1&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;{{ note.text }}&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0056","card":"q-django-014-5-class-based-views","sec":"django-s014","q":"What are Django class-based views (CBVs), and what do they need in URLs?","a":"<p>CBVs implement the common view behaviour, and you override attributes. They need <code>.as_view()</code> in URLs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0057","card":"q-django-015-templateview-and-mixins","sec":"django-s015","q":"How do you write a <code>TemplateView</code> that renders <code>home/welcome.html</code> with today's date?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.views.generic import TemplateView\n\nclass HomeView(TemplateView):\n    template_name = &#x27;home/welcome.html&#x27;\n    extra_context = {&#x27;today&#x27;: datetime.today()}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0058","card":"q-django-015-templateview-and-mixins","sec":"django-s015","q":"How do you route a class-based view such as <code>HomeView</code> in <code>urls.py</code>?","a":"<p>Call <code>.as_view()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>path(&#x27;home&#x27;, views.HomeView.as_view())   # was views.home</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0059","card":"q-django-015-templateview-and-mixins","sec":"django-s015","q":"In Django, what is a mixin, and where does <code>LoginRequiredMixin</code> go?","a":"<p>Mixins add features by combination. <code>LoginRequiredMixin</code> replaces <code>@login_required</code> and must come <strong>before</strong> the view class.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.contrib.auth.mixins import LoginRequiredMixin\n\nclass AuthorizedView(LoginRequiredMixin, TemplateView):\n    template_name = &#x27;home/authorized.html&#x27;\n    login_url = &#x27;/admin&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0060","card":"q-django-016-listview-and-detailview","sec":"django-s016","q":"How do you write <code>ListView</code> and <code>DetailView</code> classes for <code>Notes</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.views.generic import ListView, DetailView\n\nclass NotesListView(ListView):\n    model = Notes\n    context_object_name = &#x27;notes&#x27;      # default is object_list\n    template_name = &#x27;notes/notes_list.html&#x27;\n\nclass NotesDetailView(DetailView):\n    model = Notes\n    context_object_name = &#x27;note&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0061","card":"q-django-016-listview-and-detailview","sec":"django-s016","q":"How do you route <code>NotesListView</code> and <code>NotesDetailView</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>path(&#x27;notes&#x27;, views.NotesListView.as_view()),\npath(&#x27;notes/&lt;int:pk&gt;&#x27;, views.NotesDetailView.as_view()),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0062","card":"q-django-016-listview-and-detailview","sec":"django-s016","q":"What do <code>ListView</code> and <code>DetailView</code> do automatically?","a":"<p><code>ListView</code> runs <code>.objects.all()</code> itself. <code>DetailView</code> fetches by <code>pk</code> and <strong>returns 404 automatically</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0063","card":"q-django-016-listview-and-detailview","sec":"django-s016","q":"What are the default template names for <code>ListView</code> and <code>DetailView</code> in Django?","a":"<p><code>&lt;app&gt;/&lt;model&gt;_list.html</code> and <code>&lt;app&gt;/&lt;model&gt;_detail.html</code>. So <code>template_name</code> is optional when you follow the convention.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0064","card":"q-django-016-listview-and-detailview","sec":"django-s016","q":"What does <code>context_object_name</code> do in a Django <code>ListView</code>, and what is the default?","a":"<p>It names the variable the template receives. The default is <code>object_list</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0065","card":"q-django-016-listview-and-detailview","sec":"django-s016","q":"Function-based vs class-based views in Django: how do they differ?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Function-based</th><th>Class-based</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Query</td><td>Written manually</td><td>Automatic</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>404</td><td>Manual <code>try/except</code> + <code>Http404</code></td><td>Automatic</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Auth</td><td><code>@login_required</code></td><td><code>LoginRequiredMixin</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Template context</td><td>dict in <code>render()</code></td><td><code>context_object_name</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>URL</td><td><code>views.func</code></td><td><code>views.Class.as_view()</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0066","card":"q-django-016-listview-and-detailview","sec":"django-s016","q":"Which tool helps you explore class-based view attributes and methods, and when are CBVs the right tool?","a":"<p>ccbv.co.uk (Classy Class-Based Views). CBVs are the right tool in the vast majority of cases.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0067","card":"q-django-017-custom-queryset-popular-notes","sec":"django-s017","q":"How do you make a Django <code>ListView</code> show only notes with at least one like?","a":"<p>Set <code>queryset</code>, which replaces the default <code>.objects.all()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class PopularNotesListView(ListView):\n    model = Notes\n    context_object_name = &#x27;notes&#x27;\n    template_name = &#x27;notes/notes_list.html&#x27;\n    queryset = Notes.objects.filter(likes__gte=1)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0068","card":"q-django-018-static-files","sec":"django-s018","q":"What folder layout holds a Django stylesheet?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>static/\n  css/\n    style.css</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0069","card":"q-django-018-static-files","sec":"django-s018","q":"Which <code>settings.py</code> values configure Django static files?","a":"<p><code>STATIC_URL</code> exists by default, and <code>STATICFILES_DIRS</code> points to the <code>static</code> folder.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>STATIC_URL = &#x27;/static/&#x27;          # exists by default\nSTATICFILES_DIRS = [\n    BASE_DIR / &#x27;static&#x27;,\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0070","card":"q-django-018-static-files","sec":"django-s018","q":"How do you link a static CSS file in a Django template?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% load static %}\n&lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; type=&quot;text/css&quot; href=&quot;{% static &#x27;css/style.css&#x27; %}&quot;&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0071","card":"q-django-018-static-files","sec":"django-s018","q":"When is <code>{% load static %}</code> needed in Django?","a":"<p>At the top of any template that uses <code>{% static %}</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0072","card":"q-django-019-base-template-and-extends","sec":"django-s019","q":"What is the purpose of a Django base template?","a":"<p>It holds shared HTML/CSS in one place. Child templates fill a block.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0073","card":"q-django-019-base-template-and-extends","sec":"django-s019","q":"How do you tell Django where <code>base.html</code> lives?","a":"<p>Add the folder to <code>DIRS</code> in <code>TEMPLATES</code> in <code>settings.py</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>TEMPLATES = [\n    {\n        &#x27;DIRS&#x27;: [BASE_DIR / &#x27;static/templates&#x27;],\n        # ...\n    },\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0074","card":"q-django-019-base-template-and-extends","sec":"django-s019","q":"What does a Django base template with a content block and Bootstrap 5 look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% load static %}\n&lt;html&gt;\n  &lt;head&gt;\n    &lt;link href=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css&quot; rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;/head&gt;\n  &lt;body&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;my-5 text-center container&quot;&gt;\n      {% block content %}\n      {% endblock %}\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0075","card":"q-django-019-base-template-and-extends","sec":"django-s019","q":"How does a child template use the base template in Django?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% extends &quot;base.html&quot; %}\n{% block content %}\n  &lt;h1 class=&quot;my-5&quot;&gt;These are the notes:&lt;/h1&gt;\n  ...\n{% endblock %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0076","card":"q-django-019-base-template-and-extends","sec":"django-s019","q":"Is the block name <code>content</code> fixed in Django templates?","a":"<p>No. The block name is arbitrary, and <code>content</code> is the convention. Only the block content is unique per page.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0077","card":"q-django-020-named-urls","sec":"django-s020","q":"Why name URLs in Django instead of hardcoding links?","a":"<p>Hardcoded links break when deploying. Name the URLs and use <code>{% url %}</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0078","card":"q-django-020-named-urls","sec":"django-s020","q":"How do you name URL patterns in Django?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>urlpatterns = [\n    path(&#x27;notes&#x27;, views.NotesListView.as_view(), name=&#x27;notes.list&#x27;),\n    path(&#x27;notes/&lt;int:pk&gt;&#x27;, views.NotesDetailView.as_view(), name=&#x27;notes.detail&#x27;),\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0079","card":"q-django-020-named-urls","sec":"django-s020","q":"How do you link to a named URL, with and without a parameter, in a Django template?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.list&#x27; %}&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot;&gt;Check out these smart notes!&lt;/a&gt;\n&lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.detail&#x27; pk=note.id %}&quot; class=&quot;text-dark text-decoration-none&quot;&gt;{{ note.title }}&lt;/a&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0080","card":"q-django-021-styled-list-and-detail-templates","sec":"django-s021","q":"What does a styled Django notes list template look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% extends &quot;base.html&quot; %}\n{% block content %}\n  &lt;h1 class=&quot;my-5&quot;&gt;These are the notes:&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;row row-cols-3 g-2&quot;&gt;\n    {% for note in notes %}\n      &lt;div class=&quot;col&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;p-3 border&quot;&gt;\n          &lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.detail&#x27; pk=note.id %}&quot; class=&quot;text-dark text-decoration-none&quot;&gt;{{ note.title }}&lt;/a&gt;\n          &lt;p&gt;{{ note.text|truncatechars:10 }}&lt;/p&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n    {% endfor %}\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n{% endblock %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0081","card":"q-django-021-styled-list-and-detail-templates","sec":"django-s021","q":"What does <code>{{ note.text|truncatechars:10 }}</code> do in a Django template?","a":"<p><code>|</code> applies a template filter. <code>truncatechars:10</code> shows the first 10 characters plus <code>...</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0082","card":"q-django-021-styled-list-and-detail-templates","sec":"django-s021","q":"What does a styled Django note detail template look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% extends &quot;base.html&quot; %}\n{% block content %}\n  &lt;div class=&quot;border rounded&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h1 class=&quot;my-5&quot;&gt;{{ note.title }}&lt;/h1&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;{{ note.text }}&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n{% endblock %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0083","card":"q-django-022-include-partial-templates","sec":"django-s022","q":"What does <code>{% include \"home/advantages.html\" %}</code> do in a Django template?","a":"<p>It inserts a fragment inside the current template.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;h3 class=&quot;my-5&quot;&gt;Some advantages of our app:&lt;/h3&gt;\n{% include &quot;home/advantages.html&quot; %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0084","card":"q-django-022-include-partial-templates","sec":"django-s022","q":"How is a partial template such as <code>advantages.html</code> written?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;ul&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;Simple&lt;/li&gt;\n  &lt;li&gt;Powerful&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0085","card":"q-django-022-include-partial-templates","sec":"django-s022","q":"Django <code>{% extends %}</code> vs <code>{% include %}</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Tag</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>{% extends \"base.html\" %}</code></td><td>Inheritance: child builds on a parent</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>{% include \"x.html\" %}</code></td><td>Composition: insert a fragment inside the current template</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0086","card":"q-django-023-7-forms-csrf-and-validation","sec":"django-s023","q":"What is the minimum a system should support, and which Django view gives the Create part?","a":"<p>CRUD is the minimum. <strong>CreateView</strong> gives Create.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0087","card":"q-django-023-7-forms-csrf-and-validation","sec":"django-s023","q":"How do you write a <code>CreateView</code> for notes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.views.generic import CreateView\n\nclass NotesCreateView(CreateView):\n    model = Notes\n    fields = [&#x27;title&#x27;, &#x27;text&#x27;]      # `created` is auto-populated, so skipped\n    success_url = &#x27;/smart/notes&#x27;    # redirect after success</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0088","card":"q-django-023-7-forms-csrf-and-validation","sec":"django-s023","q":"Why does <code>NotesCreateView</code> leave <code>created</code> out of <code>fields</code>, and what does <code>success_url</code> do?","a":"<p><code>created</code> is auto-populated, so it is skipped. <code>success_url</code> is the redirect after success.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0089","card":"q-django-023-7-forms-csrf-and-validation","sec":"django-s023","q":"How do you route a <code>CreateView</code> with the name <code>notes.new</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>path(&#x27;notes/new&#x27;, views.NotesCreateView.as_view(), name=&#x27;notes.new&#x27;),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0090","card":"q-django-023-7-forms-csrf-and-validation","sec":"django-s023","q":"What does the Django form template <code>notes_form.html</code> look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% extends &quot;base.html&quot; %}\n{% block content %}\n  &lt;form action=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.new&#x27; %}&quot; method=&quot;POST&quot;&gt;\n    {% csrf_token %}\n    {{ form }}\n    &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary my-5&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n{% endblock %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0091","card":"q-django-023-7-forms-csrf-and-validation","sec":"django-s023","q":"What does <code>{{ form }}</code> do in a Django template?","a":"<p>It generates the HTML from the field types (<code>CharField</code> becomes <code>&lt;input&gt;</code>, <code>TextField</code> becomes <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code>) with auto labels.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0092","card":"q-django-024-csrf","sec":"django-s024","q":"What happens when a Django POST form has no <code>{% csrf_token %}</code>, and what does CSRF stand for?","a":"<p>The POST returns <strong>403 Forbidden</strong>. CSRF is Cross-Site Request Forgery.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0093","card":"q-django-024-csrf","sec":"django-s024","q":"How does Django's CSRF protection work?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>Django sends a unique token to the browser with the form page.</li>\n  <li>The token is submitted back with the data.</li>\n  <li>Django verifies it, so only the browser that got the form can submit it. A third party has no token and is rejected.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0094","card":"q-django-024-csrf","sec":"django-s024","q":"Where must <code>{% csrf_token %}</code> go in Django?","a":"<p>Inside every <code>&lt;form method=\"POST\"&gt;</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0095","card":"q-django-025-modelform-and-validation","sec":"django-s025","q":"How do you write a <code>ModelForm</code> with custom labels and widgets for <code>Notes</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django import forms\nfrom .models import Notes\n\nclass NotesForm(forms.ModelForm):\n    class Meta:\n        model = Notes\n        fields = [&#x27;title&#x27;, &#x27;text&#x27;]\n        labels = {\n            &#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;Write your thoughts here.&#x27;,\n        }\n        widgets = {\n            &#x27;title&#x27;: forms.TextInput(attrs={&#x27;class&#x27;: &#x27;form-control my-5&#x27;}),\n            &#x27;text&#x27;: forms.Textarea(attrs={&#x27;class&#x27;: &#x27;form-control my-5&#x27;}),\n        }</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0096","card":"q-django-025-modelform-and-validation","sec":"django-s025","q":"How do you add custom validation for the <code>title</code> field in a Django form?","a":"<p>Write a method <code>clean_&lt;fieldname&gt;</code>, read <code>self.cleaned_data['fieldname']</code> and raise <code>forms.ValidationError(...)</code> to reject.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def clean_title(self):\n    title = self.cleaned_data[&#x27;title&#x27;]\n    if &#x27;Django&#x27; not in title:\n        raise forms.ValidationError(&#x27;We only accept notes about Django!&#x27;)\n    return title</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0097","card":"q-django-025-modelform-and-validation","sec":"django-s025","q":"How do you make a <code>CreateView</code> use a custom form class?","a":"<p>Set <code>form_class</code>, which replaces <code>fields</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class NotesCreateView(CreateView):\n    model = Notes\n    form_class = NotesForm      # replaces `fields`\n    success_url = &#x27;/smart/notes&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0098","card":"q-django-025-modelform-and-validation","sec":"django-s025","q":"What do <code>labels</code> and <code>widgets</code> do in a Django <code>ModelForm</code> <code>Meta</code> class?","a":"<p><code>labels</code> overrides labels. <code>widgets</code> sets the HTML tag and attributes (for example Bootstrap classes). All of it is controlled from the form class without touching the template.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0099","card":"q-django-025-modelform-and-validation","sec":"django-s025","q":"How do you show form errors in a Django template, and how do you hide the default list?","a":"<p>Hide the default list with the CSS <code>ul.errorlist { display: none; }</code> and use <code>form.errors</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% if form.errors %}\n  &lt;div class=&quot;alert alert-danger my-5&quot;&gt;\n    {{ form.errors.title.as_text }}\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n{% endif %}\n{{ form }}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0100","card":"q-django-026-codespaces-csrf-fix","sec":"django-s026","q":"What error can Django show in Codespaces even with the token, and what is the fix?","a":"<p><code>CSRF verification failed</code>. Set <code>CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS</code> in <code>settings.py</code> when running in Codespaces.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import os\nCODESPACE = os.environ.get(&#x27;CODESPACES&#x27;) == &#x27;true&#x27;\nif CODESPACE:\n    CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS = [&#x27;https://localhost:8000&#x27;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0101","card":"q-django-027-updateview","sec":"django-s027","q":"How do you write an <code>UpdateView</code> for notes, and what does it reuse?","a":"<p>It reuses the same form class and <code>notes_form.html</code>, and the fields come pre-filled.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.views.generic import UpdateView\n\nclass NotesUpdateView(UpdateView):\n    model = Notes\n    form_class = NotesForm\n    success_url = &#x27;/smart/notes&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0102","card":"q-django-027-updateview","sec":"django-s027","q":"How do you route the update view for a note?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>path(&#x27;notes/&lt;int:pk&gt;/edit&#x27;, views.NotesUpdateView.as_view(), name=&#x27;notes.update&#x27;),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0103","card":"q-django-027-updateview","sec":"django-s027","q":"Why remove the hardcoded <code>action</code> from the <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> when one template serves create and edit?","a":"<p>So the form posts to the current URL.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot;&gt;\n    {% csrf_token %}\n    {{ form }}\n    &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary my-5&quot;&gt;Submit&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.list&#x27; %}&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-secondary&quot;&gt;Cancel&lt;/a&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0104","card":"q-django-028-deleteview","sec":"django-s028","q":"How do you write a <code>DeleteView</code> for notes with its own template?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.views.generic.edit import DeleteView\n\nclass NotesDeleteView(DeleteView):\n    model = Notes\n    success_url = &#x27;/smart/notes&#x27;\n    template_name = &#x27;notes/notes_delete.html&#x27;   # default would be notes_confirm_delete.html</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0105","card":"q-django-028-deleteview","sec":"django-s028","q":"What is the default template name for a Django <code>DeleteView</code>?","a":"<p><code>notes_confirm_delete.html</code> for the <code>Notes</code> model.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0106","card":"q-django-028-deleteview","sec":"django-s028","q":"How do you route the delete view?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>path(&#x27;notes/&lt;int:pk&gt;/delete&#x27;, views.NotesDeleteView.as_view(), name=&#x27;notes.delete&#x27;),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0107","card":"q-django-028-deleteview","sec":"django-s028","q":"What does the delete confirmation template look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% extends &quot;base.html&quot; %}\n{% block content %}\n  &lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot;&gt;\n    {% csrf_token %}\n    &lt;p&gt;Are you sure you want to delete &quot;{{ note.title }}&quot;?&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;This action can&#x27;t be undone.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-danger&quot; value=&quot;Confirm&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.detail&#x27; pk=note.id %}&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-secondary&quot;&gt;Cancel&lt;/a&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n{% endblock %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0108","card":"q-django-028-deleteview","sec":"django-s028","q":"How do you add Edit and Delete buttons to the note detail page?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.update&#x27; pk=note.id %}&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-secondary&quot;&gt;Edit&lt;/a&gt;\n&lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.delete&#x27; pk=note.id %}&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-danger&quot;&gt;Delete&lt;/a&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0109","card":"q-django-029-crud-map","sec":"django-s029","q":"In the SmartNotes project, which CBV, URL and template does each CRUD operation use?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>CBV</th><th>URL</th><th>Template</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Create</td><td><code>CreateView</code></td><td><code>notes/new</code></td><td><code>notes_form.html</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Read (list)</td><td><code>ListView</code></td><td><code>notes</code></td><td><code>notes_list.html</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Read (detail)</td><td><code>DetailView</code></td><td><code>notes/&lt;int:pk&gt;</code></td><td><code>notes_detail.html</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Update</td><td><code>UpdateView</code></td><td><code>notes/&lt;int:pk&gt;/edit</code></td><td><code>notes_form.html</code> (reused)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Delete</td><td><code>DeleteView</code></td><td><code>notes/&lt;int:pk&gt;/delete</code></td><td><code>notes_delete.html</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0110","card":"q-django-029-crud-map","sec":"django-s029","q":"Which template do Create and Update share in SmartNotes?","a":"<p><code>notes_form.html</code>, reused by <code>UpdateView</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0111","card":"q-django-030-like-button-function-based-view","sec":"django-s030","q":"When is a function-based view simpler than a class-based view in Django?","a":"<p>For simple actions with no input or validation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0112","card":"q-django-030-like-button-function-based-view","sec":"django-s030","q":"How do you write a like view in Django?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.http import Http404, HttpResponseRedirect\nfrom django.shortcuts import get_object_or_404\nfrom django.urls import reverse\n\ndef add_like_view(request, pk):\n    if request.method == &#x27;POST&#x27;:\n        note = get_object_or_404(Notes, pk=pk)\n        note.likes += 1\n        note.save()\n        return HttpResponseRedirect(reverse(&#x27;notes.detail&#x27;, args=(pk,)))\n    raise Http404</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0113","card":"q-django-030-like-button-function-based-view","sec":"django-s030","q":"How do you route a function-based view such as <code>add_like_view</code>?","a":"<p>Without <code>.as_view()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>path(&#x27;notes/&lt;int:pk&gt;/add-like&#x27;, views.add_like_view, name=&#x27;notes.add-like&#x27;),   # no .as_view()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0114","card":"q-django-030-like-button-function-based-view","sec":"django-s030","q":"What does the like button template look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;p&gt;{{ note.likes }} likes&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot; action=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.add-like&#x27; pk=note.id %}&quot; class=&quot;d-inline&quot;&gt;\n  {% csrf_token %}\n  &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot;&gt;Upvote&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0115","card":"q-django-030-like-button-function-based-view","sec":"django-s030","q":"What do <code>get_object_or_404</code>, <code>reverse</code> and <code>HttpResponseRedirect</code> do in Django?","a":"<p><code>get_object_or_404</code> returns the object or raises 404. <code>reverse('name', args=(pk,))</code> resolves a named URL in Python. <code>HttpResponseRedirect</code> redirects.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0116","card":"q-django-030-like-button-function-based-view","sec":"django-s030","q":"Why is the like button a POST form and not an <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> link?","a":"<p><strong>Only POST may change data; GET must never modify state.</strong> So the button is a POST form with <code>{% csrf_token %}</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0117","card":"q-django-031-foreignkey-to-user","sec":"django-s031","q":"How do you link each note to a user in Django?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.contrib.auth.models import User\n\nclass Notes(models.Model):\n    # title, text, created, likes ...\n    user = models.ForeignKey(User, on_delete=models.CASCADE, related_name=&#x27;notes&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0118","card":"q-django-031-foreignkey-to-user","sec":"django-s031","q":"What do <code>on_delete=models.CASCADE</code> and <code>related_name='notes'</code> do on a ForeignKey?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>on_delete=models.CASCADE</code></td><td>Deleting the user deletes their notes</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>related_name='notes'</code></td><td>Reverse access: <code>user.notes.all()</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0119","card":"q-django-031-foreignkey-to-user","sec":"django-s031","q":"Why does <code>makemigrations</code> ask for a one-off default after adding the <code>user</code> ForeignKey, and what do you answer?","a":"<p>Existing rows have no user. Choose option 1 and enter an existing user's pk (here 1), then <code>migrate</code>. This works only because pk=1 exists, so be careful adding required fields to tables with data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0120","card":"q-django-031-foreignkey-to-user","sec":"django-s031","q":"How do you count and list a user's notes through the reverse relation?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>user = User.objects.get(pk=1)\nuser.notes.count()\nuser.notes.all()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0121","card":"q-django-032-filter-by-logged-in-user-get-queryset","sec":"django-s032","q":"How do you make a <code>ListView</code> show only the logged-in user's notes?","a":"<p>Override <code>get_queryset</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class NotesListView(LoginRequiredMixin, ListView):\n    model = Notes\n    context_object_name = &#x27;notes&#x27;\n    template_name = &#x27;notes/notes_list.html&#x27;\n    login_url = &#x27;/admin&#x27;\n\n    def get_queryset(self):\n        return self.request.user.notes.all()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0122","card":"q-django-032-filter-by-logged-in-user-get-queryset","sec":"django-s032","q":"What is the chain of calls in a Django <code>ListView</code>, and what does the default <code>get_queryset()</code> return?","a":"<p><code>GET -&gt; get() -&gt; get_queryset() -&gt; DB query -&gt; template</code>. The default <code>get_queryset()</code> returns <code>Model.objects.all()</code>. Overriding it customises the query.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0123","card":"q-django-032-filter-by-logged-in-user-get-queryset","sec":"django-s032","q":"How do you find which method of a Django CBV to override?","a":"<p>Read the class on ccbv.co.uk (for example, ListView's <code>get</code> calls <code>get_queryset</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0124","card":"q-django-032-filter-by-logged-in-user-get-queryset","sec":"django-s032","q":"How do you get the current user in any Django CBV?","a":"<p><code>self.request.user</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0125","card":"q-django-033-assign-the-user-on-create-form-valid","sec":"django-s033","q":"Why does saving a note fail after the <code>user</code> ForeignKey is added, and how do you fix it in <code>CreateView</code>?","a":"<p>The <code>user</code> is null. Override <code>form_valid</code> and inject the logged-in user.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def form_valid(self, form):\n    self.object = form.save(commit=False)   # build object, do NOT hit the DB yet\n    self.object.user = self.request.user    # inject logged-in user\n    self.object.save()\n    return HttpResponseRedirect(self.get_success_url())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0126","card":"q-django-033-assign-the-user-on-create-form-valid","sec":"django-s033","q":"How is the full <code>NotesCreateView</code> with login protection written?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.http.response import HttpResponseRedirect\n\nclass NotesCreateView(LoginRequiredMixin, CreateView):\n    model = Notes\n    form_class = NotesForm\n    success_url = &#x27;/smart/notes&#x27;\n    login_url = &#x27;/admin&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0127","card":"q-django-033-assign-the-user-on-create-form-valid","sec":"django-s033","q":"What is the submit flow in a Django form view, and what does <code>commit=False</code> do?","a":"<p><code>is_valid()</code> runs the <code>clean_*</code> methods. If valid, <code>cleaned_data</code> is populated and <code>form_valid()</code> is called. <code>commit=False</code> lets you modify the object before saving.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0128","card":"q-django-034-public-private-toggle","sec":"django-s034","q":"Which field makes a note public or private, and how should boolean fields be named?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>is_public = models.BooleanField(default=False)</code></pre></div>\n<p>Run <code>makemigrations</code> and <code>migrate</code>. Name boolean fields as yes/no questions: <code>is_public</code> is clearer than <code>public</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0129","card":"q-django-034-public-private-toggle","sec":"django-s034","q":"How do you write a view that flips a note's visibility?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def change_visibility_view(request, pk):\n    if request.method == &#x27;POST&#x27;:\n        note = get_object_or_404(Notes, pk=pk)\n        note.is_public = not note.is_public   # flip\n        note.save()\n        return HttpResponseRedirect(reverse(&#x27;notes.detail&#x27;, args=(pk,)))\n    raise Http404</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0130","card":"q-django-034-public-private-toggle","sec":"django-s034","q":"How do you route the visibility toggle view?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>path(&#x27;notes/&lt;int:pk&gt;/change-visibility&#x27;, views.change_visibility_view, name=&#x27;notes.change-visibility&#x27;),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0131","card":"q-django-034-public-private-toggle","sec":"django-s034","q":"How does the note detail template show a Public badge and a toggle button?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;h1 class=&quot;my-5&quot;&gt;\n  {{ note.title }}\n  {% if note.is_public %}\n    &lt;span class=&quot;badge bg-secondary&quot;&gt;Public&lt;/span&gt;\n  {% endif %}\n&lt;/h1&gt;\n&lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot; action=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.change-visibility&#x27; pk=note.id %}&quot; class=&quot;d-inline&quot;&gt;\n  {% csrf_token %}\n  {% if note.is_public %}\n    &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-secondary&quot;&gt;Make Private&lt;/button&gt;\n  {% else %}\n    &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-secondary&quot;&gt;Make Public&lt;/button&gt;\n  {% endif %}\n&lt;/form&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0132","card":"q-django-035-10-login-logout-signup-public-share","sec":"django-s035","q":"How do you build login and logout pages in Django?","a":"<p>Django has built-in auth views. Wrap them and supply templates.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.contrib.auth.views import LoginView, LogoutView\n\nclass LoginInterfaceView(LoginView):\n    template_name = &#x27;home/login.html&#x27;\n\nclass LogoutInterfaceView(LogoutView):\n    template_name = &#x27;home/logout.html&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0133","card":"q-django-035-10-login-logout-signup-public-share","sec":"django-s035","q":"What are the final URL patterns of the <code>home</code> app in SmartNotes?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>urlpatterns = [\n    path(&#x27;&#x27;, views.HomeView.as_view(), name=&#x27;home&#x27;),\n    path(&#x27;login&#x27;, views.LoginInterfaceView.as_view(), name=&#x27;login&#x27;),\n    path(&#x27;logout&#x27;, views.LogoutInterfaceView.as_view(), name=&#x27;logout&#x27;),\n    path(&#x27;signup&#x27;, views.SignupView.as_view(), name=&#x27;signup&#x27;),\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0134","card":"q-django-035-10-login-logout-signup-public-share","sec":"django-s035","q":"What does the login template look like?","a":"<p><code>logout.html</code> is the same pattern with a plain message.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% extends &quot;base.html&quot; %}\n{% block content %}\n  &lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot;&gt;\n    {% csrf_token %}\n    {{ form.as_p }}\n    &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-secondary&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;/form&gt;\n{% endblock %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0135","card":"q-django-035-10-login-logout-signup-public-share","sec":"django-s035","q":"Which setting controls where Django redirects after login, and what is the default?","a":"<p><code>LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL</code>. The default is <code>/accounts/profile/</code>, which doesn't exist.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>LOGIN_REDIRECT_URL = &#x27;/smart/notes&#x27;   # default is /accounts/profile/, which doesn&#x27;t exist</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0136","card":"q-django-035-10-login-logout-signup-public-share","sec":"django-s035","q":"What should you change once a real login page exists, and what does <code>{{ form.as_p }}</code> do?","a":"<p>Change <code>login_url</code> in all views from <code>/admin</code> to <code>/login</code>. <code>{{ form.as_p }}</code> wraps each field in <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0137","card":"q-django-036-auth-aware-navbar-final-base-html","sec":"django-s036","q":"How does a Django template switch navbar buttons by login state?","a":"<p><code>user</code> is available in every template, and <code>user.is_authenticated</code> switches the buttons.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{% if user.is_authenticated %}\n  &lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.list&#x27; %}&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-outline-light me-1&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;\n  &lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;notes.new&#x27; %}&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-outline-light me-1&quot;&gt;Create&lt;/a&gt;\n{% else %}\n  &lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;login&#x27; %}&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-outline-light me-1&quot;&gt;Login&lt;/a&gt;\n  &lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;signup&#x27; %}&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-outline-light me-1&quot;&gt;Signup&lt;/a&gt;\n{% endif %}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0138","card":"q-django-036-auth-aware-navbar-final-base-html","sec":"django-s036","q":"How must logout be done in Django 5.0+, and what works in 4.x and below?","a":"<p>In Django 5.0+, logout must be POST. In Django 4.x and below, a plain link works.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">HTML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&lt;form method=&quot;POST&quot; action=&quot;{% url &#x27;logout&#x27; %}&quot; class=&quot;d-inline&quot;&gt;\n  {% csrf_token %}\n  &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-outline-light me-1&quot;&gt;Logout&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;\n&lt;!-- &lt;a href=&quot;{% url &#x27;logout&#x27; %}&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-outline-light me-1&quot;&gt;Logout&lt;/a&gt; --&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0139","card":"q-django-036-auth-aware-navbar-final-base-html","sec":"django-s036","q":"Where does the <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> sit in the base template of SmartNotes?","a":"<p>Inside <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>, before the <code>container</code> div of the base template.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0140","card":"q-django-037-signup","sec":"django-s037","q":"How do you add user registration in Django with the least code?","a":"<p>Use <code>UserCreationForm</code>, which provides registration out of the box.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from django.views.generic.edit import CreateView\nfrom django.contrib.auth.forms import UserCreationForm\n\nclass SignupView(CreateView):\n    form_class = UserCreationForm\n    template_name = &#x27;home/register.html&#x27;\n    success_url = &#x27;/login&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0141","card":"q-django-037-signup","sec":"django-s037","q":"What does the signup template look like, and what is the flow?","a":"<p><code>register.html</code> is the login form pattern with <code>value=\"Sign Up\"</code> on the submit input. The flow is: signup, redirect to login, then redirect to the notes list.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0142","card":"q-django-038-public-share-link","sec":"django-s038","q":"How do you build a public share page in Django that needs no login?","a":"<p>Use a <code>DetailView</code> whose queryset is restricted to public notes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class NotesPublicDetailView(DetailView):\n    model = Notes\n    context_object_name = &#x27;note&#x27;\n    template_name = &#x27;notes/notes_detail.html&#x27;\n    queryset = Notes.objects.filter(is_public=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0143","card":"q-django-038-public-share-link","sec":"django-s038","q":"How do you route the public share view?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>path(&#x27;notes/&lt;int:pk&gt;/share&#x27;, views.NotesPublicDetailView.as_view(), name=&#x27;notes.share&#x27;),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0144","card":"q-django-038-public-share-link","sec":"django-s038","q":"What happens when someone opens the share URL of a private note, and why is it safe?","a":"<p>It returns 404, so the note is never exposed. The filter is enforced at the query level.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"django-f0145","card":"q-django-039-11-where-to-go-next","sec":"django-s039","q":"What does the Django course suggest learning next?","a":"<p>Unit testing in Django (testing the system built here), and Django REST Framework for adding APIs.</p>","hand":true}];
